    <briefdescription>
<para>A <emphasis>classic</emphasis> code example for a <bold>GDExtension</bold> </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The class must inherit from a Godot built in class (like  <godotonly position="open" kind="text" content="["/>Object<godotonly position="close" kind="text" content="]"/>,  <godotonly position="open" kind="text" content="["/>Node<godotonly position="close" kind="text" content="]"/>,  <godotonly position="open" kind="text" content="["/>Sprite2D<godotonly position="close" kind="text" content="]"/>, or  <godotonly position="open" kind="text" content="["/>Resource<godotonly position="close" kind="text" content="]"/>). Godot does not support multiple inheritance for GDExtension classes. Why the #@# does the editor documentation allow csharp code blocks if it never displays them?</para>
<para>Example Usage: <programlisting filename=".cs"><codeline><highlight class="normal">GodotObject<sp/>sum<sp/>=<sp/>ClassDB.Instantiate(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;Summator&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">).As&lt;GodotObject&gt;();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">sum.Call(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;add&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,5);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">sum.Call(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;add&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,7);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>total<sp/>=<sp/>sum.Call(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;get_total&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">).As&lt;</highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">int</highlight><highlight class="normal">&gt;();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>prints<sp/>12</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">GD.Print(total);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> <programlisting filename=".gdscript"><codeline><highlight class="normal">var<sp/>sum<sp/>=<sp/>Summator.new()</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/>sum.add(5)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/>sum.add(7)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/>var<sp/>total<sp/>=<sp/>sum.get_total()</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/>#<sp/>prints<sp/>12</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/>print(total)</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><xrefsect id="signal_1_signal000001"><xreftitle>Signal</xreftitle><xrefdescription><para> <godotonly kind="signal" name="sum_changed(int: sum)"/><parblock><para><bold>sum_changed(int: sum):</bold></para>
<para>This <bold>signal</bold>, is <emphasis>emitted</emphasis> when the sum changes whether after adding a new integer or when resetting the total back to zero.</para>
<para></para>
</parblock></para>
</xrefdescription></xrefsect><simplesect kind="note"><para>“You&apos;re on Earth. There&apos;s no cure for that.” ― Samuel Beckett</para>
</simplesect>
</para>
<para><xrefsect id="signal_1_signal000002"><xreftitle>Signal</xreftitle><xrefdescription><para> <godotonly kind="signal" name="sum_reset()"/><parblock><para><bold>sum_reset():</bold></para>
<para>This signal is emitted when the total is reset to zero </para>
</parblock></para>
</xrefdescription></xrefsect><simplesect kind="note"><para>Gogo: &apos;We always find something, eh Didi, to give us the impression we exist?" </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>I&apos;m making this up as I go along</para>
</simplesect>
</para>
<para><xrefsect id="signal_1_signal000003"><xreftitle>Signal</xreftitle><xrefdescription><para> <godotonly kind="signal" name="doesnt_exist"/><parblock><para><bold>doesnt_exist:</bold></para>
<para>This is just a plain description, no warning or note for parser testing. This signal doesn&apos;t actually exist, so don&apos;t try to use it. This should only output to html as the signal is not actually registered with ClassDB.</para>
</parblock></para>
</xrefdescription></xrefsect></para>
<para>Check Status Example: <programlisting filename=".gdscript"><codeline><highlight class="normal">if<sp/>total<sp/>&gt;=<sp/>sum.SUM_GOOD:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>print(&quot;Life<sp/>is<sp/>good&quot;)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">elif<sp/>total<sp/>&gt;=<sp/>sum.SUM_OKAY:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>print(&quot;Could<sp/>be<sp/>doing<sp/>better&quot;)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">elif<sp/>total<sp/>&gt;=<sp/>sum.SUM_REQUIRED:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>print(&quot;At<sp/>least<sp/>you<sp/>making<sp/>rent&quot;)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">else:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>print(&quot;Your<sp/>broke&quot;)</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
